Cross-checks

These are not app-scoped and will catch content the queries above miss.

Which scheduled searches actually run

Metadata tells you what is scheduled; this tells you what is alive.

spl
index=_internal sourcetype=scheduler status=success earliest=-90d
| stats count as runs, max(_time) as last_run by savedsearch_name, app
| eval last_run=strftime(last_run, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M")
| sort - runs
Ad hoc searches against the index

Catches queries people run constantly but never saved — frequently the most important logic in the environment, and invisible to any knowledge-object export.

spl
index=_audit action=search info=granted earliest=-90d
| search "*<index>*"
| stats count, values(user) as users, max(_time) as last_seen by search
| sort - count
Content in other apps that touches this index

Structural app filtering misses relevant objects parked elsewhere.

spl
| rest /servicesNS/-/-/saved/searches count=0 splunk_server=*
| where like(lower(search), "%<index>%") AND 'eai:acl.app'!="<index>"
| table title, eai:acl.app, eai:acl.owner, eai:acl.sharing, search
